commonplace to ﬁrst construct the ﬁnite-dimensional distributions. These
are found by choosing any integer q  1, and any set of points {xk }qk=1 in
D, and then considering the random vector (u(x1 ; ·)∗ , . . . , u(xq ; ·)∗ )∗ ∈ Rnq .
